  "title": "U.S.-Venezuela Oil Deal Amid Criticism and Geopolitical Implications",
  "summary": "The U.S. announced a major oil deal with Venezuela, securing 65 billion barrels of proven oil reserves, while the U.S. claims to have majority control over Venezuela’s oil resources. The deal highlights ongoing tensions and potential economic implications. Venezuela’s interim president, Delcy Rodríguez, defends the deal, but the deal has sparked outrage in the country, with Rodríguez defending her government’s stance against the U.S. claims of control.",
